			"widgets_values":[
				"Picture 1 aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 2 aligns with the 3.000-second mark.\nSubject: flat cel colour on white, a blue-haired illustrated girl, animated on twos.\nAction: She starts upright with an open-eyed restrained closed-mouth smile, matching Picture 1. She tries briefly to hold back a laugh, then her smile opens into wholehearted laughter. Her eyes squeeze shut, her head tips back slightly and her shoulders bounce twice, with her hand on screen-right pressing gently over her upper abdomen. The shoulder motion begins to settle while she keeps the joyful open-mouthed expression of Picture 2. Her twin spiral pigtails and sleeve fabric respond after each shoulder movement and settle with a slight delay. The jaw opens and closes naturally during the laugh, keeping her face recognizable. Use expressive held drawings on twos, a clear transition from suppressed smile to laughter, and a short final settle.\nCamera: a fixed eye-level waist-up medium shot, so her face, hands and the action remain large and readable throughout the performance.\nPreserve: her facial identity and proportions, blue eyes when open, blue twin spiral pigtails, lavender ribbon wraps, white hair bows, crossed hairpins, star choker, white puff-sleeve blouse and neck bow, black straps and fitted waist, crisp hand-drawn contours, flat cel colour, the fixed medium-shot scale and the white background, a natural jaw and neck, the recognizable facial features through the changing expression, one hand over her upper abdomen and the other relaxed near her waist, and the on-twos rhythm."
